Let $T\colon\R^2\to\R^2$ be the reflection over the $y$-axis. Is $T$ invertible? If so, what is $T\inv$?

 The transformation $T$ is invertible; in fact, it is equal to its own inverse. Reflecting a vector $x$ over the $y$-axis twice brings the vector back to where it started, so $T\circ T = \Id_{\R^2}$.

